findings.what:
At the 128 px chip and in the portrait, Dunsom's carved gold mask shows near-black eye recesses, a cracked-plate relief and vertical lower seams. The overall read is skull-adjacent. It is not a horror, hockey or blank-mannequin mask:
- it is warm gold under a wide pale hat;
- it has a nose nub;
- the calm lilac robe and lantern set the context.

Odrum's base mask uses the same dark eye recesses, and the final review refuted it as horror. Owner ruling 2 applies warm inlays to Odrum Shadeprint only, so it is not a roster-wide standard. 'The last mask without ruling-2 inlays' is false: Odrum base and Noon Fair keep black slits too.

